Description: Phrase band, downbeats and bar counter from rekordbox analysis
 Like the phrase display of Pioneer players: the rekordbox song structure
 (PSSI tag in the .EXT analysis file) is shown as a coloured band at the
 bottom of the waveform overview (WOverview, <PhraseBandHeight>, default 6 px,
 0 hides it). The first downbeat (PQTZ beat number 1) marks bars in the
 scrolling waveform: downbeats 2 px wide in <DownbeatColor> (default: beat
 colour), and a "bar.beat" counter next to the play marker (allshader
 waveforms only; <ShowDownbeats>, <ShowBarCounter>, default on). Tracks
 without rekordbox data can take the beat closest to the intro start as the
 first downbeat with <DownbeatFromIntroStart>true</...> (off by default; same
 idea as upstream PR #16491).
 .
 The data is imported when a track is loaded from the Rekordbox library
 view, together with the beat grid and cues, and stored as an analysis of
 type 1001 (mixxx::TrackStructure, versioned QDataStream). No database
 schema change, no beats protobuf change: stock Mixxx ignores the extra
 analysis rows; deleting a track's analyses removes them.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
